@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option desk - Overall Architecture (eight ways in, one set of artifacts out)

actor "Trader / Developer\n(terminal)" as human
package "Ways in (agent runtimes)" as ways {
  component "Claude Code\n(reads SKILL.md,\nplugin: 6 skills, 6 commands,\n2 subagents)" as claude
  component "Codex\n(scans .agents/skills,\nsymlinked to shell/skills)" as codex
  component "Gemini CLI\n(no skill discovery:\nGEMINI.md compiles all six)" as gemini
  component "ChatGPT (browser)\nskills as knowledge only:\nno local process possible" as chatgpt
}

component "MCP server (optiondesk-mcp)\nlocal stdio, standard library only\n10 typed tools" as mcp
component "CLI (optiondesk)\nexpiries | chain | greeks | exposure\nstrategy | compare | simulate\nbacktest | forward | keys | doctor | dashboard" as cli

package "shell  -  everything that touches the outside world" as shell {
  component "Provider registry\nresolve by capability,\nnever by vendor name" as providers
  component "JSON contracts\n8 schemas + validator\n(jsonschema, stdlib fallback)" as contracts
  component "Artifact writer\natomic tmp-then-replace,\nprovenance meta block,\ndegraded and notes kept apart" as artifacts
  rectangle "engine_bridge\nTHE ONLY IMPORT OF THE ENGINE\n(boundary checkable with one grep)" as bridge #C6E9C6
}

package "engine  -  the numbers, standard library only, no network" as engine {
  component "pricing\nBlack-Scholes-Merton,\n16 Greeks, implied-vol solver\nwith identifiability guards" as pricing
  component "strategies\n17 structures, payoff engine,\noutlook tags, friction verdicts" as strategies
  component "analytics\ndealer gamma exposure, walls,\nflip, max pain, smile, ranking" as analytics
  component "simulation\nGARCH-t by MCMC,\nantithetic paths, VaR and ES" as simulation
  component "backtest\nrunner, statistics, significance,\nforward marking" as backtest
}

cloud "External market data" as ext {
  component "Yahoo\nfree, delayed,\nall capabilities, no key" as yahoo
  component "Alpha Vantage\nkey required,\nhistory and quotes,\n~25 requests/day" as av
}

database "Artifact directory\n~/TradingDesk/option-desk\n+ archive/<date>/ for every\nreplaced measurement" as disk
component "Dashboard\nFastAPI or stdlib, ECharts vendored,\nreads artifacts, writes nothing" as dash

claude --> mcp : 1. tools/call
codex --> mcp : 1. tools/call
gemini --> mcp : 1. tools/call
human --> cli : 1. subcommand
mcp --> cli : 2. same entry points
cli --> providers : 3. ask for a capability
providers --> yahoo : 4. priority order
providers --> av : 4. only if key present
cli --> bridge : 5. numbers via the bridge
bridge --> pricing
bridge --> strategies
bridge --> analytics
bridge --> simulation
bridge --> backtest
cli --> contracts : 6. validate
contracts --> artifacts : 7. write
artifacts --> disk
disk --> dash : 8. render

note right of ways
Runtime coverage:
- Claude Code: skills + commands + agents + MCP
- Codex: skills (progressive) + MCP
- Gemini: compiled docs + MCP
- Browser ChatGPT: knowledge only,
  each skill says so itself
end note

note right of engine
Engine rules:
- standard library only, no network
- testable against closed form and
  central finite differences
- a missing number is never guessed:
  iv: null is counted, not defaulted
end note

note left of bridge
The invariant:
an audit found one command importing
the engine directly. Harmless at runtime,
still routed back through the bridge:
an invariant with exceptions is not one.
end note

note bottom of disk
Nothing passes between commands
in memory. Every step is a file,
so any step can be re-run,
inspected or replaced.
end note

legend right
|= Flow |= Step |
| 1 | agent or person asks |
| 2 | MCP maps to a CLI entry point |
| 3-4 | registry resolves a provider by capability |
| 5 | engine computes through the single bridge |
| 6-7 | schema validation, atomic artifact write |
| 8 | dashboard renders what is on disk |
Tests: 829 passing, 0 skipped. Mutations: 48 run, 0 survived.
endlegend

caption Option desk: agent-driven options analytics. github.com/Iman/agent-driven-options-desk-and-skills. Research software, not investment advice.
@enduml
